  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@value": "Wikipedia (English), 'Menahem ben Solomon' (based on the Jewish Encyclopedia): 'The Sekel Ṭob, written in 1139 at Rome, is a midrashic compilation on the Pentateuch'; 25 Italian glosses indicate he lived in Italy."
   },
   {
    "@value": "Sefaria, 'Midrash Sekhel Tov' (About this text): Composed: Middle-Age Italy, 1139 CE."
   },
   {
    "@value": "Posen Library, 'Menaḥem ben Solomon': 12th century; 'It is not even known where he lived.'"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The year 1139 comes from the work itself and is not in dispute; the place (Rome/Italy) rests on internal evidence such as Italian glosses, and some sources say it is unknown."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@value": "לפי JE נכתב ברומא; הגהות איטלקיות בחיבור; Posen: מקום מגוריו אינו ידוע"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasBeginning": [
   {
