   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
   {
    "@language": "he",
    "@value": "המאה ה-5 (עד תחילת המאה ה-6)"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@value": "Encyclopaedia Judaica (2007), 'Pesikta de-Rav Kahana', on Jewish Virtual Library: 'A Palestinian text, probably of the fifth century', judged from its language and the rabbis and place names it mentions; the Shavuot and Simhat Torah chapters are later additions."
   },
   {
    "@value": "Wikipedia (English), 'Pesikta de-Rav Kahana' (cites Strack & Stemberger 1991): Probably composed in the Land of Israel; Zunz gives 700 CE, but 'other factors argue for a date of composition in the 5th or early 6th century' (citing Strack & Stemberger)."
   },
   {
    "@value": "Encyclopaedia Judaica, 'Midrash' (M. D. Herr), on Jewish Virtual Library: Its chronological table puts Pesikta de-Rav Kahana in the 500–640 block of the early (amoraic) period."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Most scholars date it to the 5th century, but Zunz put it at c. 700 (after Leviticus Rabbah), and the EJ survey table puts it in the 500–640 block; Strack & Stemberger add that the text was not finally fixed until its first printing."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@value": "מדרש אמוראי ארץ-ישראלי (לשון, חכמים ושמות מקומות)"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasBeginning": [
   {
    "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#dating_Pesikta_DRav_Kahanna_begin"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasEnd": [
   {
    "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#dating_Pesikta_DRav_Kahanna_end"
   }
  ]
 },
