   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@value": "Encyclopaedia Judaica, 'Lamentations Rabbah' (M. D. Herr), on Encyclopedia.com: 'Apparently redacted in Ereẓ Israel at about the end of the fifth century'; no sage later than the 4th century appears; it used the Jerusalem Talmud, Genesis Rabbah and Leviticus Rabbah."
   },
   {
    "@value": "Wikipedia (English), 'Lamentations Rabbah': Hasan-Rokem places it in Roman Palestine 'approximately in the middle of the first millennium'; Zunz's dating to after the mid-7th century is rebutted; it was edited after the Yerushalmi."
   },
   {
    "@value": "Posen Library, 'What Is Lamentations Rabbah?': 'Generally dated between the fifth and sixth centuries CE', with a Palestinian redaction."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Herr (EJ) dates it to about the end of the 5th century, but Zunz argued for completion no earlier than the second half of the 7th century, citing an apparent allusion to the Arab empire, an argument later rejected."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@value": "מדרש אמוראי ארץ-ישראלי; אין בו חכם מאוחר מהמאה ה-4"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasBeginning": [
   {
    "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#dating_Eichah_Rabbah_begin"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasEnd": [
   {
    "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#dating_Eichah_Rabbah_end"
   }
  ]
 },
