   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/spatial": [
   {
    "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#region_02"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
   {
    "@language": "he",
    "@value": "גרעין תנאי (המאה ה-3 לערך); עריכה סופית בתקופת הגאונים"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@value": "Wikipedia (English), 'Derekh Eretz Rabbah' (based on the Jewish Encyclopedia): A contemporary of Rebbi (c. 160–220) may have been the author; sections 1–3 added much later; the Gemara in Coronel's version is very late, probably 10th century."
   },
   {
    "@value": "M. van Loopik, The Ways of the Sages and the Way of the World (1991), preface/introduction (Mohr Siebeck PDF): Early Derekh Eretz literature dates back to the Tannaitic period, but 'presumably, the final editing did not take place until Gaonitic times'."
   },
   {
    "@value": "Encyclopaedia Judaica, 'Minor Tractates' (A. Rothkoff), on Encyclopedia.com: Some assign the minor tractates to the end of the Geonic period, but recent scholarship favors a much earlier date; Higger: mostly Palestinian, later modified in Babylonia."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The core may be tannaitic (a contemporary of Rabbi Judah ha-Nasi), but the opening chapters were added much later and van Loopik puts the final editing of the Derekh Eretz tractates in the Geonic period; some older scholars date all the minor tractates to the end of the Geonic period."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@value": "גרעין תנאי ארץ-ישראלי (לפי היגר רוב המסכתות הקטנות ארץ-ישראליות ועובדו בבבל); תוספות מאוחרות"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasBeginning": [
   {
    "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#dating_Tractate_Derekh_Eretz_Rabbah_begin"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasEnd": [
   {
