 {
  "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#dating_Midrash_Tehillim",
  "@type": [
   "http://example.org/oppenheim128#DatingAssertion",
   "http://www.w3.org/2006/time#ProperInterval"
  ],
  "http://example.org/oppenheim128#confidence": [
   {
    "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#conf_low"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/date": [
   {
    "@value": "0650/1000"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#source_eca04984a8"
   },
   {
    "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#source_22fd3dfd46"
   },
   {
    "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#source_d4a1b73550"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/spatial": [
   {
    "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#region_02"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
   {
    "@language": "he",
    "@value": "החלק העיקרי (תהלים א–קיח): המאות ה-7–ה-9/10; ההשלמה (קיט–קנ): המאה ה-13"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@value": "Encyclopaedia Judaica (2007), 'Midrash Tehillim', on Jewish Virtual Library: Zunz: edited in Italy in the last centuries of the geonic period; Buber: ancient and Palestinian; Albeck: groups of midrashim composed over 'some centuries'; the concluding section dates to the 13th century."
   },
   {
    "@value": "Wikipedia (English), 'Midrash Tehillim' (cites Friedeman & Cuénod 2021): Psalms 1–118 reached final form between the 7th and 9th centuries; Psalms 119–150 were compiled in the 13th century; edited in Palestine, and Zunz's Italy thesis is rejected."
   },
   {
    "@value": "Encyclopaedia Judaica, 'Midrash' (M. D. Herr), on Jewish Virtual Library: Its table puts Midrash Tehillim I in the middle period (640–1000; the Encyclopedia.com rendering shows the 900–1000 block) and Midrash Tehillim II in the late period (11th–12th centuries)."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "It is a layered work: Buber argued for an early Palestinian origin, Zunz for redaction in Italy late in the geonic period, and Albeck for a gradual growth over several centuries; the supplement on Psalms 119–150 is a 13th-century addition."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@value": "החלק העיקרי ארץ-ישראלי (לשון, אמוראים); צונץ הציע איטליה; ההשלמה לפרקים קיט–קנ מאוחרת (אולי ר' מתתיה היצהרי מסרגוסה)"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasBeginning": [
   {
    "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#dating_Midrash_Tehillim_begin"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasEnd": [
   {
    "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#dating_Midrash_Tehillim_end"
   }
  ]
 },
