   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
   {
    "@language": "he",
    "@value": "גרעין מן המאה ה-3 (?); עריכה סופית לא ידועה, אולי המאה ה-8"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@value": "A. Lehnardt, 'Das außerkanonische Talmud-Traktat Kutim (Samaritaner) in der innerrabbinischen Überlieferung' (Tübingen repository PDF): Via Stemberger (Einleitung in Talmud und Midrasch, 8th ed. 1992, p. 230): the core 'must have originated before the final break (with the Samaritans) at the end of the 3rd century'; Lehnardt holds that the present form must come from after the final break and rejects the early tannaitic dating of Higger and others."
   },
   {
    "@value": "Sefaria, 'Tractate Kutim' (About this text): Composed: Talmudic Israel/Babylon, 750 CE; dating and place are debated."
   },
   {
    "@value": "Encyclopaedia Judaica, 'Minor Tractates' (A. Rothkoff), on Encyclopedia.com: Kutim is one of seven brief treatises; Higger: mostly Palestinian, original composition possibly completed by 400 CE; others date them to the end of the Geonic period."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Stemberger dates a friendly core to before the final break with the Samaritans at the end of the 3rd century, while Lehnardt argues that the present text must come from after that break and calls the early dating problematic; Sefaria gives 750 CE."
   }
  ],
