   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@value": "Sefaria, 'Sifrei Aggadah on Esther' (About This Text): A collection of three midrashim on Esther prepared by Buber: Midrash Abba Gurion, Midrash Panim Aherim and Midrash Lekah Tov. It gives the place as 'Lviv' (Buber's place of work) and no composition date."
   },
   {
    "@value": "Encyclopaedia Judaica (2007), 'Midrashim, Smaller', on Jewish Virtual Library: Midrash Panim Aherim le-Esther (version A) 'was redacted not earlier than the 12th century', using Esther Rabbah II and Abba Guryon; Buber published it in the Sifrei … Esther."
   },
   {
    "@value": "Wikipedia (English), 'Midrash Abba Gorion' / EJ 'Midrash Lekah Tov' (JVL): Abba Gorion: 'no later than the ninth century' (Lerner) or 'before 1050' (Academy of the Hebrew Language). EJ (https://www.jewishvirtuallibrary.org/midrash-leka-x1e25-tov) calls Lekah Tov 'a late 11th-century Midrash' whose author lived in the Balkans; its Esther portion was published by Buber in the Sifrei de-Aggadata (1886)."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "This is Buber's 19th-century collection of three separate midrashim, each dated differently; even for Abba Gurion opinions differ ('no later than the 9th century', per Lerner, versus 'before 1050', per the Academy of the Hebrew Language)."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@value": "קובץ מודרני של בובר משלושה מדרשים: מדרש אבא גוריון (לא אחרי המאה ה-9 / לפני 1050), פנים אחרים (לא לפני המאה ה-12) ולקח טוב לר' טוביה בן אליעזר (סוף המאה ה-11, הבלקן/ביזנטיון)"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasBeginning": [
   {
    "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#dating_Sifrei_Aggadah_on_Esther_begin"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasEnd": [
   {
    "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#dating_Sifrei_Aggadah_on_Esther_end"
   }
  ]
 },
