    "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#region_09"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
   {
    "@language": "he",
    "@value": "המאה ה-11 (ר' משה הדרשן) – עריכה מאוחרת יותר, כנראה המאה ה-11/12"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@value": "Encyclopaedia Judaica, 'Genesis Rabbati' (J. Elbaum), on Encyclopedia.com: Usually ascribed to Moses ha-Darshan of Narbonne (first half of the 11th century); published from the only extant manuscript by Albeck (Jerusalem, 1940); Epstein (followed by Albeck) held it is an abridgment of 'the large Genesis Rabbah', which was the work of an anthologist who used some of Moses' work."
   },
   {
    "@value": "Wikipedia (English), 'Moshe ha-Darshan': Moses ha-Darshan c. early 11th century, head of the yeshiva of Narbonne; Zunz holds the midrash was his work, Epstein that its final compiler was 'certainly not Moses ha-Darshan'."
   },
   {
    "@value": "Sefaria, 'Bereshit Rabbati' (About this text): Often attributed to 11th-century R. Moshe HaDarshan; may have been compiled by a later editor."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Zunz attributed it to Moses ha-Darshan himself, while Epstein and Albeck see it as an abridgment by a later anonymous compiler who used Moses' work (no firm date for that final compilation was found in the sources seen)."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@value": "נרבונה – בית מדרשו של ר' משה הדרשן (מחצית ראשונה של המאה ה-11)"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasBeginning": [
   {
    "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#dating_Bereshit_Rabbati_begin"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasEnd": [
   {
    "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#dating_Bereshit_Rabbati_end"
   }
  ]
 },
