 {
  "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#dating_Bamidbar_Rabbah",
  "@type": [
   "http://example.org/oppenheim128#DatingAssertion",
   "http://www.w3.org/2006/time#ProperInterval"
  ],
  "http://example.org/oppenheim128#confidence": [
   {
    "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#conf_medium"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/date": [
   {
    "@value": "1150/1230"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#source_8c645eca05"
   },
   {
    "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#source_5f1931964f"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/spatial": [
   {
    "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#region_08"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
   {
    "@language": "he",
    "@value": "חלק א' – לא לפני אמצע המאה ה-12; חלק ב' – המאה ה-9; צורפו בתחילת המאה ה-13"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@value": "Encyclopaedia Judaica, 'Numbers Rabbah' (M. D. Herr), on Encyclopedia.com: For Part I (sections 1–14), 'the middle of the 12th century seems to be indicated as the earliest possible date', with Moses ha-Darshan of Narbonne as its main source; most scholars put Part II (sections 15–23) in the 9th century; a copyist joined the two at the beginning of the 13th century."
   },
   {
    "@value": "Wikipedia (English), 'Numbers Rabbah' (Jewish Encyclopedia-based): Zunz says it is hardly older than the 12th century, and the EJ also gives the 12th century; it was unknown to Nathan b. Jehiel and Rashi but cited by Nahmanides; the two parts differ in origin."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "The two parts differ in date and origin: Part II is a 9th-century Tanhuma-type midrash, while Part I is late (Zunz: hardly before the 12th century) and depends on Moses ha-Darshan; the two were joined by a copyist around the start of the 13th century."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@value": "חלק ב' (פרשות 15–23) הוא חומר תנחומא (ממוצא ארץ-ישראלי); חלק א' (פרשות 1–14) בנוי על מדרש ר' משה הדרשן מנרבונה (פרובנס), ולא נקבע מקום עריכתו"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasBeginning": [
   {
    "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#dating_Bamidbar_Rabbah_begin"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasEnd": [
   {
    "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#dating_Bamidbar_Rabbah_end"
   }
  ]
 },
