   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/source": [
   {
    "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#source_bbcab24c62"
   },
   {
    "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#source_e793c047f4"
   },
   {
    "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#source_1d352e2e3d"
   }
  ],
  "http://purl.org/dc/terms/spatial": [
   {
    "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#region_08"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
   {
    "@language": "he",
    "@value": "עריכה לאחר חתימת הבבלי, כנראה המאה ה-9 (פרקים א-ד קדומים)"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote": [
   {
    "@value": "Wikipedia (English), 'Derekh Eretz Zutta' (based on the Jewish Encyclopedia): Sections 5–8 are by one editor after the completion of the Babylonian Talmud; 'one would not be far wrong in setting the 9th century as the date of composition'; sections 1–4 much earlier; Perek ha-Shalom very late."
   },
   {
    "@value": "M. van Loopik, The Ways of the Sages and the Way of the World (1991), preface/introduction (Mohr Siebeck PDF): DEZ I–III(IV) roughly dates to Tannaitic times, but the final editing presumably took place in Gaonitic times."
   },
   {
    "@value": "Sefaria, 'Tractate Derekh Eretz Zuta' (About this text): Composed c. 100 BCE – c. 900 CE."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note": [
   {
    "@language": "en",
    "@value": "Chapters 1–4 may be a tannaitic collection while chapters 5–8 were edited after the Bavli; the 9th-century dating is inferred from Halakhot Gedolot, and van Loopik puts the final editing in the Geonic period."
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
   {
    "@value": "פרקים א-ד אולי תנאיים; פרקים ה-ח מעורך אחד שהכיר את הבבלי; 'פרק השלום' מאוחר מאוד"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasBeginning": [
   {
    "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#dating_Tractate_Derekh_Eretz_Zuta_begin"
   }
  ],
  "http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasEnd": [
   {
    "@id": "http://example.org/oppenheim128#dating_Tractate_Derekh_Eretz_Zuta_end"
   }
  ]
 },
